Content:
:ibox:No Foreign Merchant Ship may communicate with the Shore without `text(first)` getting the Governor's permission;

All Foreign Merchant Ships near the Shore are expected to have their National Flags flying;

Foreign Merchant Ships that want to land passengers or obtain refreshments may land near the Fort, in order to obtain the Permission of the Governor;

No Foreign Merchant Ship may take off any person, or persons, without legal permission, on pain of prosecution;

No Foreign Boats can land in the Night, except in cases of greatest emergency.
